    "result": "Perfect! All public exports are intact. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite by making minimal changes to the source code:\n\n### Issue 1: Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` Named Export\n**File**: `src/finetune/index.js`\n\nThe test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added explicit named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n### Issue 2: Toxicity Metric Receiving Wrong Arguments\n**File**: `src/eval/metrics.js`\n\nThe `toxicityMetric` function signature is `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outs, refs)`. This caused the references array to be incorrectly used as banned terms. I modified `DEFAULT_METRICS` to wrap the toxicity metric in a function that only passes the outputs parameter, allowing it to use the default banned terms.\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\npnpm --filter frai-core build\n> No build step needed - ES modules\n\npnpm --filter frai-core test\n\u2713 8 Test Files passed (8)\n\u2713 28 Tests passed (28)\nDuration: 288ms\n```\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, all public exports remain available, and no test files were modified.",
